    <Cell ss:StyleID="s17"><Data ss:Type="String">Stated Asset Allocation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="s17"><ss:Data ss:Type="String"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><Font html:Color="#000000">Investment in Equity and equity related securities *-</Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000"> 20 - 50 %&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">(*Equity Related Instruments include derivative position, convertible debentures, convertible preference shares, warrants carrying the right to obtain equity shares, units of Real Estate Investment Trust and  such other instrument as may be specified by the Board from time to time)</Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">;&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">Investment in Debt and money market instruments **- </Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">20 - 65 %&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">(**Money Market instruments include commercial papers, commercial bills, treasury bills, Government  securities having an unexpired maturity upto one year, call or notice money, certificate of deposit,  usance bills, and any other like instruments as specified by the Reserve Bank of India from time to time. This allocation includes Liquid, Overnight and other Debt mutual fund schemes. At any given time, the  total exposure to debt and money market instruments including unhedged shorts shall not exceed 65%  of the total AUM</Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">);&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">Short exposure through unhedged derivative positions in equity and debt instruments -</Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000"> 0 - 25 %&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">Units issued by InVITs - </Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">0 - 20 %&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">Commodity derivatives @ - </Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">0 - 25 %&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">(@Includes Exchange Traded Commodity Derivatives (ETCDs) such as Gold, Silver and other commodities as permitted by SEBI from time to time.)</Font><B><Font
        html:Color="#000000">&#10;</Font></B><Font html:Color="#000000">&#10;</Font></ss:Data></Cell>
